[en.C04_DESC]
Since the dissolution of the Wonderbolts in Cloudsdale, most of the dissatisfied pegasi have resisted the rule of the Empire in various ways, forming the “Free Cloudsdale Movement” to fight against the Royal Commission that came to take over. When the resistance in Cloudsdale entered a depressed period, one group after another of residents who still yearn for freedom moved to the small town of Stratusburg on the northern border, making a once obscure town lively. The “Free Cloudsdale Movement” evolved into the more enduring but gentle “Free Stratusburg Movement”. Here, they established a free and united community, following the rules set by the Empire with minimal compliance and maximum non-cooperation.

The Empire did not really care about Stratusburg, or rather, it did not care about any such small and insignificant area. After all, their taxes and contributions were zero, and the trouble they caused was also zero. But what the Empire was really afraid of was that other regions would follow the example of Stratusburg, which would make the Empire’s rule a mess. But just as the Wonderbolts eventually disbanded no matter how brilliant they were, so shall Stratusburg move forward no matter how comfortable it is. Although the public of Stratusburg are satisfied with the nominal submission to the Empire in exchange for subsidies without any strings attached, Spitfire and many of the former participants in the “Free Stratusburg Movement” understand that the Empire is always lurking, waiting for their mistakes.

[en.PIHC_WS_C04_desc]
Since the dissolution of the Wonderbolts in Cloudsdale, most of the dissatisfied pegasi have resisted the rule of the Empire in various ways. In the Greater Cloudsdale area, residents and workers in Cloudsdale, Weather Factory, and Rainbow Factory, etc., have launched one round of resistance after another. The former Wonderbolts members have become the main force leading these movements, forming the “Free Cloudsdale Movement” to fight against the Royal Commission that came to take over. The Empire could not tolerate these riots, and soon sent the newly established army of Equestria to suppress the Greater Cloudsdale area. As the main cities of the Greater Cloudsdale area were successively controlled, the rule of the Royal Commission and the Empire in the Greater Cloudsdale area gradually stabilized, and the resistance in Cloudsdale entered a depressed period. One group after another of residents who still yearn for freedom moved to the small town of Stratusburg on the northern border, making a once obscure town lively.

Stratusburg is alos a rebel region... but rebelliousness doesn’t always mean violence. The leaders appointed by the Royal Commission were neglected by the residents of Stratusburg as soon as they arrived — there was no conflict, no riot, no hostility, just neglect. Since Stratusburg was not yet named on the map, the Empire did not even notice this disobedient little town at first, let alone send police and troops to suppress it. The ponies of Stratusburg lived their lives as usual, going to work, eating and sleeping, but they never paid a single bit of tax and continued to ignore any orders from the Commission. As more and more members of the “Free Cloudsdale Movement” moved to Stratusburg, the “Free Cloudsdale Movement” evolved into the more enduring but gentle “Free Stratusburg Movement”. Here, they established a free and united community, following the rules set by the Empire with minimal compliance and maximum non-cooperation. In the following two years, the intense resistance in various regions of Greater Cloudsdale attracted most of the Empire’s attention, and the resistance forces there were gradually eliminated and assimilated by the Empire. Meanwhile, Stratusburg, as a base for moderate opposition movements, was completely ignored by the Empire due to its tranquility on the surface.

Since the signing of the Canterlot Pact, the Empire has implemented nominal elections in various territories and began to pay attention to Stratusburg, hoping to include it in the Cloudsdale constituency. The Empire’s intention was to try to shift the conflict between the pegasi of Cloudsdale and Stratusburg, and let them balance each other. In the end, the Empire succeeded halfway — the conflict did shift, but the “Free Stratusburg Movement” led by Spitfire, the former Wonderbolt captain, successfully brought the elections in Cloudsdale to a halt. After signing the ridiculous agreement with Derpy Hooves as the elected Duchess of Cloudsdale, as part of the footnote of the agreement, the “Stratusburg”, which was only mentioned twice, finally obtained their long-awaited autonomy. Spitfire was elected as the leader of the Dominion of Stratusburg. In the following two years, the Dominion of Stratusburg relied on Cloudsdale to extract huge subsidies from the Empire, but never paid a single bit of tax to the Empire. The Empire did not really care about Stratusburg, or rather, it did not care about any such small and insignificant area. After all, their taxes and contributions were zero, and the trouble they caused was also zero. But what the Empire was really afraid of was that other regions would follow the example of Stratusburg, which would make the Empire’s rule a mess.

But just as the Wonderbolts eventually disbanded no matter how brilliant they were, so shall Stratusburg move forward no matter how comfortable it is. Although the public of Stratusburg are satisfied with the nominal submission to the Empire in exchange for subsidies without any strings attached, Spitfire and many of the former participants in the “Free Stratusburg Movement” understand that the Empire is always lurking, waiting for their mistakes: the military power of Stratusburg is weak, the unity of the public and the economic backwardness are the fundamental reasons for their survival till today: the estimated income that the Empire can obtain from conquering Stratusburg is not enough to make up for the cost of suppression. This also means that once Stratusburg becomes prosperous, or the Empire finally decides to eliminate dissenters at all costs, Stratusburg will have no chance of survival.

